# Best way to **finish the task now** (without a big redesign)

Since you want to **finish the task now** and keep the redesign for later, the **simplest clean finish** is:

1. **Generate the report file on the target host**  
2. **Also show a short summary in the AAP job output**  

That avoids execution-environment `/tmp` confusion and gives you something you can prove easily. Because AAP centralizes job output/history, printing a summary there is very useful for demonstration and validation. [1](https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-02-21-create-credentials-awx/view)[3](https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_ansible_automation_platform/2.7)[4](https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/ssh-keygen.1.html)

